cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or protocol, please cite the accompanying article."
title: "certify-feature-reduction: a pre-registered, leakage-safe protocol for certifying feature-reduced clinical risk models"
abstract: >-
  Research compendium for a study auditing what the conventional AUROC-based justification for
  feature reduction misses in clinical risk modelling. Sweeps the retained-feature budget across
  twelve public clinical datasets, three feature rankers and three learners, and certifies each
  reduced model on calibration, selective reliability, clinical net benefit, conformal
  informativeness and subgroup equity under a leakage-safe protocol with paired,
  multiplicity-corrected, bootstrapped comparisons.
